    },
    {
      "name": "Amaruk Kayshapanta",
      "type": "Person",
      "isolated_context": "Amaruk Kayshapanta is an Ecuadorian multidisciplinary artist known in Spain and Ecuador for his artistic and humanistic trajectory favoring the Human Rights of Immigration in Spain. He was named the \"Chasqui de Oro\" in the VI Race and hike \"El Chasqui-NY\". He received the award \"Cultural Ambassador of the Andes-Mushuk Nina 2014 (Third Edition)\" for rescuing traditions and culture of the Andes for Indigenous Organizations of Peru, Bolivia based in Ecuador. He obtained the prize \"100 Latinos Madrid\" from the Community of Madrid to recognize his non-profit altruistic and cultural work benefiting foreign immigrants in Spain. He is known for playing the character \"Edgar\" in the TV series \"Hospital Central\". His Philosophy is named \"Amawtica Amarukiana Desestructuration\", which presents the Philosophical study of the Andean Worldview, a spiritual legacy of transformation and balance intended for awakening a collective conscience."
